# CI / VHS workflow matrices

**`vhs.yml` is hand-maintained; `ci.yml` is dynamic.** Adding a lib without updating the `all=(...)` array means the GIF never re-renders.

- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — every matrix (test / coverage / phpstan / windows-test / macos-test) is computed by `scripts/affected-libs.php` in the `build-matrix` job and consumed via `fromJSON(needs.build-matrix.outputs.*)`. The script auto-discovers libs (any dir with `composer.json` + `phpunit.xml`) and walks the reverse-dep graph from each `composer.json`'s `require[sugarcraft/*]`. Adding a lib usually needs **no** ci.yml change. Hand-maintained inside the script: `WINDOWS_LIBS`/`MACOS_LIBS` pools and `PHP_VERSIONS`.
- `ci.yml` special cases — `sugar-crush` test + coverage cells shard via `scripts/parallel-tests.sh` (K = cores, capped at 4) from `scripts/parallel-tests-durations.tsv`, fail-closed against the pinned `sugar-crush/tests/Config/Support/suite-figure.json`; coverage shards merge via `scripts/merge-clover.php`. `path-repo-check` ends with `php tools/check-child-lifetimes.php`. The `tools-guards` job name is pinned by `tools/tests/CheckPathReposTest.php` — rename both together.
- `.github/workflows/vhs.yml` — hand-maintained `all=(...)` bash array around line ~51-64. Once a lib is in the array, every `.vhs/*.tape` it owns auto-renders. Don't commit rendered GIFs — the `commit` job does that.
- `.github/workflows/sync-sugarcraft.yml` — pushes each subdir to `github.com/sugarcraft/<slug>`. Run `./scripts/bootstrap-org-repos.sh` first.
- `.github/workflows/tests.yml` — SVN credentials HARDCODED. Do NOT refactor to `${{ secrets.SVN_USER }}` — secrets don't exist in repo settings yet.

**Cache keys**: bump EVERY `-vN-` key in lockstep (`vendor-vN`, `vendor-cov-vN`, `vendor-stan-vN`, `vendor-win-vN`, `vendor-mac-vN`) — a partial bump leaves a shadowed `vendor/` re-resolving to the stale lock.

**VHS tape rules**: `Env COLUMNS "100"` (quote ALL values, even numerics). Always `Set Theme "TokyoNight"`. See `sugar-bits/.vhs/spinners.tape` for canonical shape.

**Non-visual libs exempt**: `candy-pty`, FFI bindings, codecs — skip both tape AND matrix; note exemption in PR body.
